      "rule": "No applied corner board. There is no structural post at the corner to conceal or to trim around at all — the corner is the interlocking, notched log ends themselves (see corner_quoin), and the whole point of the joint is that it stays exposed and projecting, not boxed.",
      "note": "CASCADE-PROVENANCE FIX (reasoning only; the binding outcome was already correct): the inherited germanic-vernacular forbidding reasons from 'the structural corner post is exposed... not concealed under trim' — a Fachwerk-frame concept this log (Blockbau) building does not have. Restated here with this node's own construction reality; corner_quoin (specified at nordic-alpine-vernacular) already states the correct log-notch mechanism.",
